{"slug": "kale-and-ricotta-salata-salad", "nyt_id": 1015589, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1015589-kale-and-ricotta-salata-salad", "name": "Kale and Ricotta Salata Salad", "author": "Kim Severson", "description": "This sharp and refreshing salad takes only minutes to put together but is a crowd-pleaser of the first order. This dish would be equally at home at a potluck or as a first course at a dinner party, and no one has to know that you didn’t work for hours on it.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 10, "raw": {"total": "PT10M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 bunch of Tuscan (lacinato) kale", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "bunch", "item": "of tuscan kale", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 big shallot, chopped fine", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "big shallot", "preparation": "chopped fine", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "The juice of a lemon (preferably Meyer), about 2 two tablespoons", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "the juice of a lemon", "preparation": "about 2 two tablespoons", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Salt and pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "¼ cup of olive oil, or more", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "of olive oil", "preparation": "or more", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 cup ricotta salata, coarsely shredded", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "ricotta salata", "preparation": "coarsely shredded", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Trim the leaves of the kale above where the stems become thick. (You're going to eat this raw; steam the stems for another use if you like.) Stack the leaves in a pile, 